Hi Avery,

Aisha Rahman, staff writer at Freight & Factory Journal. I'm working on a piece about how mid-market manufacturers are actually putting AI on the plant floor, as opposed to how vendors describe it, and Tessera has come up in two of my interviews (a scheduler at a Central Valley food plant and a procurement lead who would not let me quote her). I'd like to include you.

I have two questions, and either written answers or ten minutes by phone would work:

1. What is the most common reason a plant-floor AI pilot stalls before it reaches production?
2. What does "working" look like six months after go-live, in numbers a plant manager would recognize?

I'm filing Thursday 3pm Pacific. If there is a customer who would speak on the record for fifteen minutes - Northstar or Halberd came up by name - an intro would make the piece much stronger, but I understand if that is a bigger ask than the timeline allows.

Anything you'd rather keep off the record, just say so and I will honor it.

Thanks,

